      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GAS LANTERN (1) is a talented type and proved too classy last time to win by a head at Horsham in a handy 23.81 beating Fireworks. Makes plenty of appeal on the back of that last-start win. POP POP BANG (6) was well supported last time and gave a sight after a fast early split but could manage only the minor money, finishing a 2.25 lengths second (22.28) over 390m at this track. Expecting another good run. PAW YARIS (2) missed the frame latest when seventh at Sandown (30.12) but was a winner four back in the best time of the program. Should be in this for a long way. RIVIA UMIKO (8) has won at this course and distance – one to keep very safe.",
